**Generative AI Fundamentals**
* Your company launches an AI assistant that produces convincing but incorrect answers about internal policies. How would you investigate the failures, reduce unsupported claims, and measure the impact of your changes?
* A business team wants to automate an entire workflow using Generative AI, but many steps require exact calculations and policy enforcement. How would you separate generative tasks from deterministic logic?
* A proof of concept performs well in demos but fails with real customer requests. How would you build a representative evaluation dataset and decide whether the issue is prompts, data, model choice, or architecture?
* An AI feature receives positive user feedback but produces occasional high-impact errors. How would you define acceptable risk, escalation rules, and production-release criteria?

**Large Language Models (LLMs)**
* A customer-facing LLM starts producing repetitive answers after a model upgrade. How would you isolate whether the cause is model behavior, prompt changes, decoding settings, or conversation-state handling?
* An LLM answers correctly in isolation but fails when integrated into a microservice workflow. How would you investigate payload formatting, context construction, response parsing, and retries?
* An LLM provider introduces a new model version and existing regression tests begin failing. How would you compare outputs, prioritize failures, and plan rollout or rollback?
* Your application serves multiple enterprise customers, and one tenant's requests consume a disproportionate share of model capacity. How would you implement quotas, usage tracking, and fair resource allocation?

**Transformer Architecture**
* A long-document summarization service becomes significantly slower as document length increases. How would you investigate attention complexity, context length, chunking, and alternative processing strategies?
* An LLM's latency increases sharply during concurrent requests, even though average prompt length is unchanged. How would you investigate KV-cache memory, batching, scheduling, and GPU utilization?
* A model performs well on short prompts but loses important relationships in very long prompts. How would you evaluate context extension, retrieval, and long-context processing strategies?
* A self-hosted model runs out of GPU memory while processing long conversations. How would you determine whether the primary cause is model weights, KV cache, batch size, or concurrent requests?

**Attention Mechanism and Self-Attention**
* A model becomes too slow when users submit long documents. How would you determine whether attention computation or other inference stages dominate latency?
* A custom Transformer implementation produces different outputs from a reference model. How would you investigate attention masks, tensor dimensions, scaling, and positional encodings?
* A model trained on packed sequences appears to learn relationships across unrelated examples. How would you investigate causal and segment masking?
* An attention optimization improves throughput but slightly degrades model quality. How would you design benchmarks and decide whether the trade-off is acceptable?

**Tokenization and Tokens**
* An application unexpectedly exceeds its token budget after users paste source code containing unusual symbols and long identifiers. How would you investigate tokenizer behavior and improve budget estimation?
* A provider changes its tokenizer, causing a sharp increase in API costs. How would you measure the impact, adjust limits, and protect existing service-level objectives?
* Multilingual prompts use significantly more tokens than equivalent English prompts and exceed context limits. How would you investigate model-specific tokenization and design a mitigation?
* A document chunking pipeline splits important code blocks or tables at arbitrary token boundaries. How would you redesign chunking to preserve structure while respecting token limits?

**Embeddings**
* Enterprise search begins returning irrelevant documents after an embedding model is upgraded. How would you investigate vector compatibility, preprocessing, indexing, and retrieval evaluation?
* A vector index contains embeddings generated by two incompatible model versions. How would you detect the problem and plan a safe re-embedding and migration process?
* Search quality is poor for product codes and exact identifiers even though semantic queries work well. How would you introduce sparse retrieval or hybrid search and validate the improvement?
* An embedding service becomes a performance bottleneck during bulk document ingestion. How would you investigate batching, concurrency, rate limits, and indexing throughput?

**Context Windows**
* A conversation assistant begins forgetting important details after long interactions. How would you investigate truncation, history summarization, context prioritization, and external memory?
* An LLM API rejects requests because the combined system instructions, conversation history, and retrieved passages exceed the context limit. How would you design token-budget enforcement and graceful recovery?
* An assistant ignores relevant evidence buried in a long document even though the entire document fits in context. How would you investigate context ordering, retrieval, and evidence placement?
* A team increases context size to avoid chunking, but costs and latency rise substantially. How would you compare long-context processing with targeted retrieval?

**Temperature, Top-P, and Sampling**
* A structured extraction service begins returning inconsistent field values across repeated requests. How would you investigate temperature, sampling, prompt ambiguity, and output validation?
* A creative-writing feature produces repetitive content after a configuration change. How would you evaluate sampling parameters without sacrificing relevance or coherence?
* An audit requires reproducible AI-generated reports, but outputs vary between runs. How would you manage model versions, decoding configuration, and deterministic post-processing?
* A model provider changes generation behavior without an application release. How would you detect the regression and isolate the effect of model-side changes?

**Model Parameters and Quantization**
* A self-hosted LLM exceeds available GPU memory during deployment. How would you estimate memory requirements and compare quantization, smaller models, and hardware scaling?
* A quantized model fits on the target machine but performs worse on domain-specific tasks. How would you diagnose quality loss and compare alternative quantization settings?
* A model serves requests with acceptable single-user latency but slows down under concurrency. How would you benchmark throughput, KV-cache pressure, and batching behavior?
* A team proposes using the smallest quantized model to minimize infrastructure costs. How would you determine whether its quality and safety are sufficient for the intended workload?

**Pre-training, Fine-tuning, and Inference**
* A fine-tuned support model performs better on new support tickets but worse on general instructions. How would you investigate catastrophic forgetting and adjust the fine-tuning strategy?
* A team fine-tunes a model to answer internal policy questions, but answers become outdated whenever policies change. How would you compare fine-tuning with retrieval-based grounding?
* Training and evaluation metrics look strong, but inference results differ in production. How would you investigate preprocessing, model artifacts, tokenizer versions, and runtime configuration?
* A new model requires too much memory for the production serving environment. How would you evaluate quantization, distillation, batching, and alternative deployment options?

**Open-Source vs Proprietary Models**
* Your proprietary model provider experiences an outage during peak business hours. How would you route traffic to a fallback model while controlling compatibility and quality risks?
* An enterprise customer prohibits sending confidential information to external AI providers. How would you evaluate self-hosted models, private networking, and data-governance requirements?
* A self-hosted open-weight model has lower API costs but requires a large GPU fleet and ongoing maintenance. How would you compare total operating cost with a hosted service?
* A model's license changes or its provider announces deprecation. How would you assess compliance, migration options, and continuity risks?

**Multimodal AI**
* A document assistant gives an incorrect answer because it misinterprets a chart embedded in a PDF. How would you investigate image resolution, OCR, visual reasoning, and evidence verification?
* A video summarization service misses events that are visible only briefly. How would you investigate frame sampling, timestamps, temporal coverage, and context limitations?
* A multimodal assistant produces a response that contradicts the supplied image and transcript. How would you diagnose cross-modal grounding and define a reliable evaluation process?
* A multimodal API becomes expensive when users upload long videos and high-resolution images. How would you optimize preprocessing, sampling, resolution, and model routing?

**Image, Audio, Video, and Code Generation**
* An image-generation feature produces visually inconsistent results after a model update. How would you compare model versions, prompts, sampling settings, and evaluation examples?
* A voice assistant generates speech that mispronounces product names. How would you evaluate pronunciation controls, text normalization, domain adaptation, and output quality?
* AI-generated video has acceptable visual quality but inconsistent objects between frames. How would you investigate temporal consistency and determine whether the model is suitable for production?
* An AI coding assistant generates code that passes basic tests but contains a security vulnerability. How would you design sandboxing, static analysis, dependency checks, and release gates?
* Generated content triggers copyright or impersonation concerns. How would you introduce provenance checks, safety filters, human review, and incident handling?

**Model Selection and Benchmarking**
* Two models perform similarly on a public benchmark, but one fails on your company's real customer data. How would you build a representative evaluation set and compare production suitability?
* A larger model produces better answers but violates latency and cost limits. How would you evaluate smaller models, quantization, caching, and routing strategies?
* An AI provider claims a new model is significantly better, but internal evaluations show mixed results. How would you validate the claim and decide whether to migrate?
* A model performs well in offline tests but degrades after deployment. How would you combine online feedback, monitoring, regression tests, and rollback criteria?
* Different teams evaluate models with inconsistent prompts and metrics, producing conflicting recommendations. How would you establish a standardized benchmarking process?

